Z||000000||Gokart||05-17-99||05:34 AM||||I was told when I bought my red 87 GT the previous owner just put a new coat of factory red on it. It looks great but the one difference I noticed when I see other cars identical to mine is they have gray ground effects and mine match the rest of the car! How 'bout yours?
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||05-17-99||12:14 PM||||AFAIK, all Fiero's are two-toned. My red Fiero also has gray ground effects (no, I will not post that picture of my Fiero <i>again</i> ;) ). I'm not to fond about the standard gray - it's a bit too light for my taste. I had mine re-painted with a darker shade of gray and it looks a whole lot better IMO.
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||05-17-99||07:04 PM||||ALL but 88 GTs have grey skirts even the 85 GTs. Then in 86 they added the SE(which i have) that looks just like the 85 GT they painted the skirts black.
Z||000003||theogre||05-17-99||07:26 PM||||All factory SE/GT trim is gray on the colored cars as far as I can find. The only GT,SE setup I've seen that is all one color is black.<p>
Z||000004||sluppy123||05-17-99||07:50 PM||||I have a 87' GT. It's black with grey ground effects. I've seen one factory black 87' that was all black.
Z||000005||kel||05-17-99||08:11 PM||||I have a silver 86SE (with the original paint job), but the factory trim is black.
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||05-17-99||08:46 PM||||Factory GTs except 88 have grey ground effects! 86 and 87 SEs came from the factory with black ground effects! The 88 GTs came from the factory solid colors! My car is an 86 SE sliver with black ground effects! Unless the car has been painted it should fall into one of those catagories!
Z||000007||SCCA FIERO||05-17-99||08:49 PM||||NICE CAR KEL!!!!!!    :)
Z||000008||kel||05-17-99||10:28 PM||||SCCA FIERO<p>Thanks, and ditto to you.  HOWEVER, did I just read in another post that you're thinking of taking the spoiler off your 86SE to put on an 88 coupe?  Guess Fieros looking like mine are getting rarer all the time!!!
Z||000009||SCCA FIERO||05-18-99||12:11 AM||||kel, yeah i plan to sacrafice this car to make a better one. Only because it has been hit a couple of times and it just isn't straight anymore. I have had this car for a long time and the only thing i had go wrong is the clutch slave cylinder bracket broke. I hate to do this but I autocross and i want the better suspension found on the 88. I live in Utah near Salt Lake City and I have only seen a couple of "our" cars. Plenty of the gold ones and other colors but hardly any silver. I saw one about a month ago and followed the lady driving it to the store she stopped at. I asked her if she would consider selling it and she said NEVER! It was in mint condition and even the same year as mine. She bought the car new and has taken very well care of it. I guess if I can't have at least someone like her does. Maybe one day i will find another one. It wouldn't be the same becuae of the momories I have with my car though. Take care of it and have fun!
